This software and its source code, documentation, designs and assets (the
"Software") are proprietary and confidential to Co-op (the "Licensor").

Unlike an open-source licence, this notice grants NO rights by itself. Co-op
is a commercial product whose revenue comes from the licences it issues (see
the Product Requirements Document, Chapter 1 — "Primary revenue comes from
software licenses"), so access is granted per business through an activation
key issued by the Licensor and activated in Co-op → Settings → Licence.

1. GRANT. Subject to a valid, unexpired, unrevoked activation key for your
   business, the Licensor grants you a non-exclusive, non-transferable right
   to install and use the Software for your own internal business operations.

2. RESTRICTIONS. Except where mandatory law says otherwise, you may not:
   copy, redistribute, publish, sublicense or sell the Software; remove or
   alter proprietary notices; reverse engineer, decompile or disassemble it;
   share one activation key between separate businesses; or use it to build
   a competing product or service.

3. OWNERSHIP. The Software is licensed, not sold. All title, copyright and
   other intellectual property rights remain with the Licensor. You keep all
   rights in the business data you put into Co-op — the Licensor claims no
   ownership of it.

4. TERM AND REVOCATION. The right to use continues while your activation key
   is valid. The Licensor may revoke a key (for non-payment, breach, or a
   chargeback); revocation takes effect immediately and ends this grant.

5. NO WARRANTY. The Software is provided "as is", without warranty of any
   kind, express or implied, including merchantability, fitness for a
   particular purpose and non-infringement.

6. LIMITATION OF LIABILITY. To the maximum extent permitted by law, the
   Licensor is not liable for indirect, incidental, special, consequential
   or punitive damages, or for lost profits, revenue or data, arising from
   the use of or inability to use the Software.

7. THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS. The Software incorporates open-source libraries
   (listed in frontend/package.json, electron/package.json and
   backend/requirements.txt), each under its own licence. Nothing here
   restricts your rights under those licences.

For licensing questions, or to obtain a key, contact the Co-op team.

